{
  "description": "Shared Rust/WASM vector for the PowerShell command builder (#298). Every expected value is written by hand from the rules in crates/allw-core/src/powershell.rs (argv is always a whitespace split of raw; risk floor Medium; High when raw contains ; | & a line break, a backtick, ( {, [scriptblock] or .invoke, a nested-execution command word (iex, Invoke-Expression, Invoke-Command, icm, Start-Process, start, saps, Start-Job, sajb, powershell, pwsh, cmd), an -EncodedCommand parameter or prefix (or -ec), led by one or two of - / U+2013 U+2014 U+2015, with every quote character in the token ignored (or only the quoted segment it starts with), a command named like PowerShell itself (a name starting pwsh or powershell, after any path and with its quotes removed), or dot-sourcing (a leading . word, or . directly followed by a quote or $); raw verbatim); never regenerate it from program output.",
